WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.307
ALEX: So. One billion dollars. AMD takes
a one-billion-dollar quarterly charge
tied to

00:00:04.307 --> 00:00:08.614
ALEX: its AI chip supply agreements with
OpenAI and Meta. Reuters has this.

00:00:08.614 --> 00:00:12.921
ALEX: And I want to get the accounting
right, because a charge isn't

00:00:12.921 --> 00:00:17.228
ALEX: the same as losing a billion
dollars outright, is it?

00:00:17.313 --> 00:00:20.386
JAMIE: And it's specifically the OpenAI
and Meta deals. Not general overhead.
This

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:23.459
JAMIE: is the price of being their
chipmaker.

00:00:23.569 --> 00:00:26.688
ALEX: So AMD locked in these agreements,
committed to supplying at a certain

00:00:26.688 --> 00:00:29.806
ALEX: scale, and the accounting weight
of that lands as a billion-dollar hit

00:00:29.806 --> 00:00:32.925
ALEX: in a single quarter.
